WEBVTT

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:17.200
"Planet Shummoor
Day 25 of being lost in space"
Team B5 camp log,
day one on Planet Shummoor.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:20.330
After successfully averting the crash,

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:24.160
we have arrived safely on Planet Shummoor,
the second planet of our trip.

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:30.700
I'm so excited, I'm starting to get dizzy!

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.870
Hey! No! I understand how you feel.
But now is not the time for this!

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:54.500
Sorry, I failed to check the "in use" sign.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:00.080
Get dressed. We're landing soon.

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:03.080
Huh?!

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:04.750
Aye, yeah!

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:08.200
Yes, I said "Aye, yeah" too, right then.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.910
Is that a healthy reaction
to seeing a girl naked?!

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:12.120
I've seen that before.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:14.200
It's completely different!
There are curves and stuff!

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:17.700
--What's this "aye, yeah" I keep hearing?
--Are you an idiot?! Or an idiot?!

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:21.660
Luca, you gotta see my anime.

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:24.790
It's a phrase Beego says
to mean "understood."

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:29.080
That sounds good, we should use it too.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:32.370
I was feeling kind of weird about
saying "understood" to Kanata.

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:33.870
Hey, what?!

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:41.250
I'm still surprised we made it.
I thought we were done for.

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:45.950
Me, too. I thought our
hidden enemy was behind it.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:50.000
But we're all alive.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.950
Um...

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:57.500
I was thinking, even if there is
an enemy hiding among us,

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:01.580
perhaps that person is doing
their best to survive right now.

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:05.410
If that's the case, we should have
the enemy continue to help us.

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:09.450
We need all the help we can get
to work on various survival tasks.

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:11.290
What do you think, captain?

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:14.000
Same as before.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.790
Don't overthink things you can't know.

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:21.330
The most dangerous thing is, we doubt
each other and teamwork falls apart.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:24.540
Once we lose control,
we're seriously done for.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:27.370
From here on, we're all prohibited
from trying to find the enemy.

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:28.370
Understood?

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:30.410
Aye, yeah!

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:38.120
To the enemy hiding here,
I say, do your worst!

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:39.870
And seriously, who is it anyway?!

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:42.370
I thought we're not going
to try to find the enemy.

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:49.540
I wonder what 0.85G gravity is like?

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:52.450
It should be noticeable, but not much more.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:53.910
It shouldn't be disorienting.

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:55.450
Oh, no, no.

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:57.660
I read in a manga

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:00.620
that my body should feel real light, and even
a slight jump would launch me way up.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:02.580
Exciting, isn't it?

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:06.750
Landing on Planet Shummoor!

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:07.790
What?!

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:10.250
Kanata's sinking!

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:13.200
Parts of the ground are soft and fluffy.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:14.950
This must be moss.

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:17.040
That's what you get for
jumping in without checking.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:17.830
Are you an idiot?

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:21.580
No! It was intentional!
A spectacular gag for a spectacular landing!

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:24.080
So, we've landed, but...

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:26.540
The view is quite lonely.

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:28.750
There'd better be food here.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:31.200
I'm not eating moss and stuff.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:36.200
There must be something edible here,
but finding it could be an issue.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.790
Oh, no...

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:43.870
No, that's not what a captain should say.

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:45.620
Let's enjoy this, as much as possible.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:49.790
We are lost in space, but it is a super
unique and valuable planet camp too.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:52.250
Let's split into two teams and look for food.

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:53.700
Planet exploration!

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.870
Aye, yeah!

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:01.910
Is that edible?

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:04.370
"Food search team:
Kanata, Aries, Luca, Zack"
Like a wild vegetable?

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:06.870
It's slightly glowing. How pretty.

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:08.580
Let's check it out.

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:09.660
Yummy!

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:11.370
Yes! "Yummy"!

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:13.830
Wait, was that Funi's voice?

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:15.700
Yeah, I improved it.

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:17.450
What a meaningless improvement!

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:21.290
This better be okay.

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:23.080
The sensor says it's delicious.

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:25.120
By whose standards?!

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.370
Kanata!

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.410
"Delicious!"
Delicious!

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:32.290
"Delicious!"
Huh?!

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:35.790
It tastes like every tasty thing
I've ever eaten, joined together!

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:38.700
That has to be an exaggeration.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:40.540
"Delicious!"
Delicious!

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:43.660
I'm naming these "Candy Plants."

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:46.830
Let's grab the ones growing around here
and bring them back for the others.

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:49.620
Yes, it's very delicious!

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:51.500
How many are you eating, Aries?!

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:53.620
Zacky boy, come sit and eat with us.

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:55.160
Stop treating me like you're my mother!

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:58.000
Sheesh, seriously...

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:02.700
Guys, take a look.

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:05.950
Wow, is that a satellite?

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:12.080
I've never seen anything so exciting!

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:15.750
Space is awesome!

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:24.080
I knew it, this cactus is full of water.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:26.000
"Water search team:
Ulgar, Charce, Quitterie, Funicia, Yunhua"
I knew it, this cactus is full of water.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.830
"Water search team:
Ulgar, Charce, Quitterie, Funicia, Yunhua"
Water problem, solved in a flash!

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:29.330
Water problem, solved in a flash!

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:31.290
This is promising.

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:33.950
Let's grab a few and bring them back.

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:36.120
How are we supposed to carry this stuff?

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:39.250
We can go back and bring
the anti-gravity carry carts.

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:40.950
Hey, big girl.

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:43.830
We don't know which ones are
fit for long-term storage.

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:46.500
Stop getting too many of one type.

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:48.660
You're so useless.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.160
I know...

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:55.080
I really do know.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:59.830
Hey look, there's a bunch of different types
of vegetables growing here.

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:04.290
It seems to center around
that pole-shaped tree.

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:05.910
Quitterie, um...

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:07.120
It stinks!

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:09.370
What?! It's not me!

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:11.910
It does smell quite bad...

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:12.950
There!

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:14.700
An animal carcass.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:20.750
The moss on this plant seems
to feed on animal carcasses.

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:23.120
See, this whole area...

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:24.330
...it's full of dead animals.

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:27.160
No!

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:30.200
Tooth shapes indicate herbivores!

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:34.660
Wow, there's no stopping this guy...

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:36.910
If there are dead herbivores....

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:38.120
Hmm?

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:39.910
There could be carnivores, too!

00:06:39.910 --> 00:06:42.950
I wanna see them! Eat them! Dissect them!

00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:45.700
Why are you so excited?!

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:49.290
What if they're violent?

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:51.910
What if they eat us?!

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:54.250
Hey, stop, Funicia...

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:58.200
It's here!

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:02.250
He wants to be friends with you, Quitterie.

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:06.620
--Space creature! Hey, Charce! Charce!
--Here, have some vegetables.

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:07.950
Yes. It's here.

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:08.700
"Tremble"
Yes. It's here.

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.290
"Tremble"
I can't stand this guy!

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:16.250
He wants you to hop on.

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:17.330
Huh?

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:22.330
Hiyah!

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:24.200
It's like I'm in a dream!

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:27.040
I'd love to wake up now!

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:30.290
Oh, riding on the back of a creature
that's never been seen before,

00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:33.580
riding off into an uncharted land...

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:35.580
My dream come true!

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:41.660
Wow, you brought back quite a party.

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:43.750
They're called Gruppies.

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:47.290
Funi fed them some vegetables,
and they offered to give us a ride.

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:48.450
They're quite honorable.

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:49.910
Repaying debts!

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:50.790
Yes!

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:53.450
How is it so easy for them to accept this...?

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:55.080
I got us some water.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:58.120
Unfortunately there was only
a little bit of food...

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:02.580
We got tons of food. See? Hmm...

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:04.370
Something stinks.

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:05.620
Quitterie, did you pass gas?

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:07.040
Kaboom!

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:11.790
Are you an idiot?!
I've never passed that in my entire life!

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:13.290
That's a lie.

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:17.290
I've never drop-kicked anyone in my life,
but I pulled it off just fine!

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:22.910
Ouch, 0.85G sure adds
to the flight distance...

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:26.330
These dried up plants--is this the food?

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:28.330
This must be where
the smell is coming from.

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:29.620
Rotten!

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:31.870
It's inedible.

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:35.870
Seems like the Candy Plants
spoil unnaturally fast.

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:38.290
It's not suitable for storage.

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:41.040
Oh, no...

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:50.700
These are the only plants that
are edible and fit for storage.

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:54.620
Just for reference, Gruppies are not
suitable as a food source.

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:56.160
Don't eat them!

00:08:57.620 --> 00:09:00.200
How much food do we have on board?

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:04.660
Three days' worth...
Maybe five if we conserve.

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:16.040
We've found some safe plants.
Maybe there are some edible animals, too!

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:17.290
Right, Aries?

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:18.250
"Grumble"

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:21.750
Don't reply with your stomach!

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:23.040
Hey.

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:28.080
Shouldn't we just get the minimum amount
of food and move on to the next planet?

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:30.750
The calculation is already
based on bare minimums.

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:33.910
It would be tough to conserve even more.

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:37.000
If we run out of food in space,
we'd be doomed.

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:41.790
I'm sure you're having the time
of your life here, Dr. Animal Lover!

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:42.620
Please, please...

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:43.700
Kanata.

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:45.450
Yeah.

00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:48.450
We're not taking off until we
reach the target amount.

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:54.000
Let's cut our meals by 30% and
conserve water. No bathing or laundry.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:57.790
But let me say I'm sorry I already
started washing the jacket I spoiled.

00:09:57.790 --> 00:09:59.160
What?!

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:02.870
So I guess this is going to be
a tough trip after all.

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:05.620
Can we get through this by just conserving?

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:08.660
I get a feeling Yunhua might eat a lot...

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:09.830
Hey, Luca!

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:12.750
Sorry! I'm going to bed now.

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:14.370
I'll rest, too.

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:18.200
I said don't respond with your stomach...

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:25.870
"Planet Shummoor
Day 26 of being lost in space"

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:31.950
Dang, it's not dry yet.

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:33.950
Kanata!

00:10:33.950 --> 00:10:36.080
It's Yunhua, she...

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:41.040
"I will stay on this planet.
Please leave me here"...?

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:43.910
She left a note?

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:46.950
Yunhua...

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.250
Quitterie, you're in charge.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:54.580
I understand.

00:10:54.580 --> 00:10:56.540
Yunhua!

00:10:56.540 --> 00:11:00.080
--Yunhua!
--Yunhua!

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:04.700
It's my fault. I said those things
to her yesterday...

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:06.910
I've said similar things.

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:07.830
Huh?!

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:08.910
Like "big girl."

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:12.370
Hey! Maybe you caused this!

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:15.160
Shut up. It's your fault.

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:25.700
I get a feeling Yunhua might eat a lot...

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:29.370
Idiot. What is this, a sacrifice?

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:30.830
Yunhua!

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:56.000
♪ Don't be scared. Don't be scared. ♪

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:59.830
♪ Don't be scared of the friends
in the forest. ♪

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:01.790
Lead role in the class play?

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:04.370
Yes! I was chosen.

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:07.450
Singing? You?

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:09.200
Yes...

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:11.540
I told them not to let her do anything...

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:14.120
Get out of the play.

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:16.750
I'll speak with the teacher for you.

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:18.500
You can't handle it.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:21.540
You'll just fail and cause trouble.

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:24.660
Go get a role where
you don't draw attention.

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:28.750
♪ Don't be scared. Don't be scared. ♪

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:32.660
♪ Don't be scared of the friends
in the forest. ♪

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:36.330
Yunhua!

00:12:39.790 --> 00:12:41.040
Wait!

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:43.750
Please wait!

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:50.410
You can't beat me at running!

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:54.870
Arm drag?!

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:02.660
I'll stay away from you.
We can talk via helmet communicator.

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:08.330
You left your glasses on the ship.

00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:10.580
I don't need them, they're...

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:12.040
Non-prescription, right?

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:14.870
Aries noticed.

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:17.750
Kanata, look.

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:20.370
Is Yunhua okay without them?

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:22.450
She'll be fine.

00:13:22.450 --> 00:13:25.790
They're just for fashion.

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:30.450
You think people don't pay
attention to you, right?

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:34.040
In fact, people look out for you.
We're all companions.

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:38.080
You just wear the glasses to keep
your bangs out of your eyes, right?

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:42.120
And the bangs are there to hide your face?

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:45.540
I want to show as little of myself as possible.

00:13:45.540 --> 00:13:48.540
I'm so useless... Yet I'm so big.

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:51.000
But you don't have to just up
and leave like this.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:54.580
I'm of no help to anyone.

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:57.660
Everyone else has a special talent.

00:13:57.660 --> 00:14:01.160
It hurts so much... To be so useless...

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:03.790
You don't need a flashy talent

00:14:03.790 --> 00:14:06.450
just help the others out.

00:14:07.410 --> 00:14:10.080
I'm sorry, I...

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:12.540
I don't want to fail and draw attention.

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:15.040
I don't like succeeding and
drawing attention either.

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:18.330
If you can't do anything right,

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:20.950
the least you could do is stay out of sight.

00:14:20.950 --> 00:14:23.870
That's how I was raised.

00:14:23.870 --> 00:14:26.950
To express myself is a shameful thing.

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:29.500
What...?

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:32.660
I...

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:36.660
I want to be invisible.

00:14:42.330 --> 00:14:44.290
The wind is getting stronger.

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:47.660
Oh, Zack, Funi.

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:50.120
Still no luck?

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:53.750
Let's go back to the ship and restart.

00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:57.330
The temperature is falling.
We should put on our crust suits.

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:07.620
Charce.

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:10.040
Over there...

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:12.870
Ah, it's spreading its seeds.

00:15:12.870 --> 00:15:15.750
Or more like spores, perhaps?

00:15:15.750 --> 00:15:20.500
Perhaps these Pole Trees are similar to ferns.

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:23.330
Aries?!

00:15:27.450 --> 00:15:30.370
Everyone... Don't breathe...

00:15:31.750 --> 00:15:33.450
These spores are poisonous...

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:41.450
I should have seen this coming,
from all of the poisonous plants here...

00:15:41.450 --> 00:15:45.250
This planet... is ruled by...

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:46.950
...mushrooms...

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:56.250
The wind is getting stronger.

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:02.000
What's wrong?

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:03.500
You hungry?

00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:08.040
Yunhua...

00:16:08.040 --> 00:16:12.450
I found this by that tree over there.

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:14.250
Maybe he'll eat this.

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:20.000
Good, you're all healthy now!

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:25.450
Survival tip number 7: eat and get energy.

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:28.290
Yunhua, let's go back and eat something.

00:16:31.450 --> 00:16:32.750
What's up?

00:16:32.750 --> 00:16:34.910
Ka... nata...

00:16:36.290 --> 00:16:38.500
Charce! What's going on?!

00:16:39.250 --> 00:16:43.950
Good... You're wearing your helmet...

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:46.750
Come to this location immediately...

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:50.660
Keep your helmet on...!

00:16:53.830 --> 00:16:55.620
Quitterie, are you there?!

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:57.080
Them, too?

00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:59.950
Luca and Ulgar came back dying too.

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:07.160
It seems like the Pole Trees have
spores with fast-acting poisons.

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:11.910
Symptoms are high fever,
coughing, muscle pains...

00:17:11.910 --> 00:17:13.750
Can you cure this?!

00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:16.660
I don't know! Don't ask me!

00:17:16.660 --> 00:17:18.540
You're the only one!

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:23.370
Please, Quitterie!
You're the ship's doctor!

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:29.540
I'll do what I can. I'm laying them down
on the bridge, bring mattresses!

00:17:29.540 --> 00:17:30.830
Got it!

00:17:33.160 --> 00:17:35.330
We can talk later!

00:17:35.330 --> 00:17:36.830
Give me a hand.

00:17:36.830 --> 00:17:38.000
Yes!

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:41.700
Poison mushrooms?

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:47.870
Yes, they have strong poisons,
and use spores to spread.

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:50.620
It's only a hypothesis, but...

00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:54.200
It would not be out of the question
for a fungus, codependent with plants,

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:59.410
to have poisons designed
to actively kill animals.

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:03.250
The moss grows on the animal carcass,

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:07.660
which photosynthesize energy
for the mushroom to grow.

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:11.540
Those mushrooms are the rulers of this planet.

00:18:13.950 --> 00:18:19.910
They're not recovering. The supplies
on this ship simply aren't enough...

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:24.330
Tell me, Charce. There has to be
a balance in the ecosystem.

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:28.790
The plants and mushrooms must not want
to kill too many animals, right?

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:36.040
Yes, it's possible that they use some
method to control how many they kill.

00:18:36.040 --> 00:18:38.950
What method?

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:41.750
Like an antidote, for example.

00:18:41.750 --> 00:18:45.790
A medicinal mushroom would not
be out of the question.

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:46.870
Kanata!

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:51.370
That thing we fed the Gruppie...

00:18:51.370 --> 00:18:54.410
Maybe that was a medicine mushroom?

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:04.290
Yes! That must have been it!

00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:07.950
But I only saw one in that location...

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:14.660
We know there's a cure for this.

00:19:14.660 --> 00:19:16.410
I'll find some and bring them back!

00:19:17.160 --> 00:19:18.450
The root...

00:19:19.540 --> 00:19:20.790
Root of the Pole Trees?

00:19:20.790 --> 00:19:27.080
Yes... How do they place
the carcasses around themselves?

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:30.370
Maybe they lure them close
with the medicine...

00:19:30.370 --> 00:19:32.040
I get it!

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:38.750
The sick animals go to
the Pole Trees to get medicine.

00:19:38.750 --> 00:19:40.790
If they find it, they're cured.

00:19:40.790 --> 00:19:44.080
If not, they die there.

00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:49.870
That ratio is controlled by the Pole Tree...

00:19:59.870 --> 00:20:01.120
No!

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:03.950
There aren't any medicine mushrooms!

00:20:03.950 --> 00:20:06.500
What is this?!

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:09.700
Quitterie!

00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:12.700
You have the symptoms, too!

00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:14.330
What can I do...?

00:20:14.330 --> 00:20:18.200
Without Quitterie, there's nothing I can...

00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:23.500
I haven't done anything except
make them feel a bit better.

00:20:23.500 --> 00:20:26.750
All we can do is wait for Kanata.

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:37.910
New footprints... But no new carcasses.

00:20:37.910 --> 00:20:42.040
Were all the medicine mushrooms
eaten already...?

00:20:42.040 --> 00:20:46.830
No. I must not have the right to find them,
since I'm not showing the symptoms.

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:15.040
I hate that word, "hopeless."

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:22.540
You're lying, you don't want to be invisible!

00:21:22.540 --> 00:21:25.660
There must be something
you really want to become!

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:40.000
♪ I used to be like a bird in a cage. ♪

00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:43.000
--Someone's singing...?

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:46.540
--♪ I would never fly ♪
--Someone's singing...?

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:47.870
--♪ or rest on a forest branch. ♪
--A singer?!

00:21:47.870 --> 00:21:49.540
--♪ or rest on a forest branch. ♪
--Your dream is to become a singer?

00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:52.660
--♪ or rest on a forest branch. ♪
--Don't yell so loud!

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:55.120
--My mother told me not to tell others.

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:57.080
--♪ But one night, ♪
--My mother told me not to tell others.

00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:58.500
--♪ But one night, ♪
--She said I shouldn't sing in front of others either.

00:21:58.500 --> 00:22:00.750
--♪ I dreamed of a boat on the waves ♪

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:01.540
--♪ I dreamed of a boat on the waves ♪
--But I still love my mother when she sings.

00:22:01.540 --> 00:22:04.370
--♪ and wondered ♪
--But I still love my mother when she sings.

00:22:04.370 --> 00:22:07.830
♪ what lay past ♪

00:22:07.830 --> 00:22:09.080
I love singing.

00:22:09.080 --> 00:22:16.290
♪ what I could see. ♪

00:22:16.950 --> 00:22:19.750
--♪ I cut the long hair ♪

00:22:19.750 --> 00:22:22.160
--♪ I cut the long hair ♪
--Because...

00:22:22.160 --> 00:22:24.290
♪ that wrapped round my body. ♪
--...it's very soothing.

00:22:24.290 --> 00:22:28.580
♪ The time for me to fly had come! ♪

00:22:28.580 --> 00:22:35.200
♪ I flew through the specks of light ♪

00:22:35.200 --> 00:22:41.540
♪ and turned a flip in the air. ♪

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:42.950
♪ "Goodbye!" I called out. ♪

00:22:42.950 --> 00:22:49.200
♪ I have chosen my destination -- ♪

00:22:49.200 --> 00:22:55.790
♪ the lemon-colored star of hope. ♪

00:22:55.790 --> 00:23:00.750
♪ The excitement in my chest is rising, ♪

00:23:00.750 --> 00:23:07.040
♪ but I am not afraid. I squint my eyes ♪

00:23:07.040 --> 00:23:13.370
♪ at the bright light. I kick the ground ♪

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:18.500
♪ as I start to run, ♪

00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:22.950
♪ using the flowers as my runway. ♪

00:23:32.540 --> 00:23:34.950
Team B5 camp log.

00:23:34.950 --> 00:23:39.580
A bunch of things happened, but we were
all saved by the medicine mushrooms

00:23:39.580 --> 00:23:41.790
that Kanata brought back.

00:23:43.750 --> 00:23:47.080
Great work, Kanata...
